@startuml
skinparam titleFontSize 16
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #FCE4EC
skinparam arrowColor #333333

title How an API Key Becomes Request Headers

actor "User with API Key\n(sk-abc...)" as User
rectangle "Envoy AI Gateway" as Envoy #E1F5FE
rectangle "Authorino\n(ext_authz, order 5)" as Auth #E1F5FE

rectangle "Keycloak\n(token exchange)" as KC #FFF3E0
rectangle "Lightbridge API\n(authz service)" as LB #E8F5E9
database "Lightbridge DB\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB #FCE4EC

User -> Envoy : Request + API Key
Envoy -> Auth : 1. Authenticate
Auth -> KC : 2. Exchange key for token
KC -> LB : 3. Lookup key metadata
LB -> DB : 4. SELECT project, plan, model_policy...
DB --> LB : Row: project data
LB --> KC : billing_plan, model_policy, balance...
KC --> Auth : Identity + project claims
Auth --> Envoy : 5. Stamp headers onto request:
note right of Envoy
  Headers stamped on every request:
  ─────────────────────────────────
  x-billing-plan: pro
  x-account-id: proj-abc
  x-model-policy: allowlist
  x-allowed-models: gpt-4o,claude-3-5-sonnet
  x-billing-period: 2026-10  (Lua stamps this)
  ─────────────────────────────────
  Dynamic metadata (internal only):
  budget.remaining_micros: 8457487
  budget.decision: allow
  budget.known: true
  budget.enforced: true
end note
@enduml
